  <section itemprop="claims" itemscope>
    <h2>Claims (<span itemprop="count">10</span>)</h2>
    
    <div itemprop="content" html><div mxw-id="PCLM23418537" lang="EN" load-source="patent-office" class="claims">
    <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00001" num="00001" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">1. An isolated antibody or antigen-binding fragment thereof, which specifically binds human interleukin-4 receptor (hIL-4R) comprising the amino acid sequence of SEQ ID NO: 274, comprising a heavy chain variable region comprising three heavy-chain CDRs, and a light chain variable region comprising three light-chain CDRs, wherein said three heavy-chain CDRs comprise the CDR1, CDR2 and CDR3 from SEQ ID NO:162, and said three light-chain CDRs comprise the CDR1, CDR2 and CDR3 from SEQ ID NO:164.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00002" num="00002" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">2. The antibody or antigen-binding fragment of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein said heavy chain CDR1 comprises SEQ ID NO:148, said heavy chain CDR2 comprises SEQ ID NO:150, said heavy chain CDR3 comprises SEQ ID NO:152, said light chain CDR1 comprises SEQ ID NO:156, said light chain CDR2 comprises SEQ ID NO:158, and said light chain CDR3 comprises SEQ ID NO:160.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00003" num="00003" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">3. The antibody or antigen-binding fragment of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00002">claim 2</claim-ref>, wherein said heavy chain variable region comprises SEQ ID NO:162.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00004" num="00004" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">4. The antibody or antigen-binding fragment of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00002">claim 2</claim-ref>, wherein said light chain variable region comprises SEQ ID NO:164.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00005" num="00005" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">5. A pharmaceutical composition comprising the antibody or antigen-binding fragment of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref> and a pharmaceutically acceptable carrier.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00006" num="00006" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">6. The pharmaceutical composition of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00005">claim 5</claim-ref>, wherein said heavy chain CDR1 comprises SEQ ID NO:148, said heavy chain CDR2 comprises SEQ ID NO:150, said heavy chain CDR3 comprises SEQ ID NO:152, said light chain CDR1 comprises SEQ ID NO:156, said light chain CDR2 comprises SEQ ID NO:158, and said light chain CDR3 comprises SEQ ID NO:160.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00007" num="00007" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">7. The pharmaceutical composition of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00006">claim 6</claim-ref>, wherein said heavy chain variable region comprises SEQ ID NO:162.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00008" num="00008" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">8. The pharmaceutical composition of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00006">claim 6</claim-ref>, wherein said light chain variable region comprises SEQ ID NO:164.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00009" num="00009" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">9. An antibody or antigen-binding fragment thereof, which specifically binds human interleukin-4 receptor (hIL-4R) comprising the amino acid sequence of SEQ ID NO: 274, comprising a heavy chain variable region comprising SEQ ID NO:162 and a light variable region comprising SEQ ID NO:164.</div>
    </div>
    </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00010" num="00010" class="claim">
      <div class="claim-text">10. A pharmaceutical composition comprising the antibody or antigen-binding fragment of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00009">claim 9</claim-ref> and a pharmaceutically acceptable carrier.</div>
    </div>
  </div> </div>
  </div>
  </section>

